1. `trinity-compress.config.json` — configuration with rules and targets
2. `scripts/trinity-compress.sh` — the main compression bash script
3. Makefile with `optimize-prompts` and `optimize-undo` targets
4. `.gitignore` update to ignore `*.bak`
5. `scripts/install.sh` and `scripts/install.ps1` installer scripts

The script should compress prompt files, create .bak backups, and support undo functionality.",
  "plan": "Create the scripts directory and all required files:
1. Create scripts directory
2. Create trinity-compress.sh with compression, backup, and undo functionality
3. Create trinity-compress.config.json
4. Create install.sh and install.ps1
5. Create/update Makefile
6. Create/update .gitignore
7. Make the bash script executable",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "mkdir -p scripts\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > trinity-compress.config.json << 'EOF'
{
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "name": "trinity-compress",
  "description": "Pre-run prompt compression for iterative AI dev loops",
  "targets": {
    "prompt_files": ["*.md", "*.txt", "prompts/*.md", "prompts/*.txt"],
    "exclude": ["node_modules", ".git", "*.bak", "dist", "build"]
  },
  "modes": {
    "balanced": {
      "description": "Balanced compression with readability",
      "remove_whitespace": true,
      "collapse_redundancy": true,
      "preserve_code": true
    },
    "aggressive": {
      "description": "Maximum compression, may reduce clarity",
      "remove_whitespace": true,
      "collapse_redundancy": true,
      "preserve_code": false
    },
    "light": {
      "description": "Minimal compression, maximum clarity",
      "remove_whitespace": false,
      "collapse_redundancy": false,
      "preserve_code": true
    }
  },
  "backup": {
    "enabled": true,
    "extension": ".bak",
    "retention": "last_run"
  }
}
EOF\n",
